{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-callbacks_and_events-typescript-repair-01","problem":"Repair the implementation below and return one complete TypeScript source file.

Export exactly this API:

```ts
export type MutationListener = (
  items: string[],
  done: (error?: Error) => void,
) => void;

export type PipelineComplete = (
  error: Error | null,
  snapshots: readonly (readonly string[])[],
) => void;

export function runMutationListeners(
  source: readonly string[],
  listeners: readonly MutationListener[],
  complete: PipelineComplete,
): void;
```

`runMutationListeners` must invoke listeners sequentially. A listener begins only after the preceding listener calls its `done` callback successfully. Every listener must receive a fresh mutable copy of the original `source`; mutations made by one listener must neither alter `source` nor appear in another listener's input. After each successful listener, save an immutable copy of the array it produced. When all listeners succeed, call `complete(null, snapshots)` once with snapshots in listener order.

If a listener reports an error or throws before acknowledging, stop the pipeline and call `complete` once with that error and only the snapshots from previously successful listeners. Convert a non-`Error` thrown value with `new Error(String(value))`. Ignore repeated calls to the same listener's `done`, and ignore a throw that occurs after that listener has already acknowledged. With no listeners, complete immediately with an empty snapshot array.

The implementation must be self-contained and deterministic. Do not use filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. It must compile under strict TypeScript as CommonJS targeting ES2022.

The current source incorrectly aliases listener inputs:

```ts
export type MutationListener = (
  items: string[],
  done: (error?: Error) => void,
) => void;

export type PipelineComplete = (
  error: Error | null,
  snapshots: readonly (readonly string[])[],
) => void;

export function runMutationListeners(
  source: readonly string[],
  listeners: readonly MutationListener[],
  complete: PipelineComplete,
): void {
  const snapshots: (readonly string[])[] = [];
  const payload = [...source];
  let index = 0;
  let finished = false;

  const finish = (error: Error | null): void => {
    if (finished) return;
    finished = true;
    complete(error, Object.freeze([...snapshots]));
  };

  const advance = (): void => {
    if (finished) return;
    if (index === listeners.length) {
      finish(null);
      return;
    }

    const listener = listeners[index++];
    let acknowledged = false;

    const done = (error?: Error): void => {
      if (acknowledged || finished) return;
      acknowledged = true;
      if (error !== undefined) {
        finish(error);
        return;
      }
      snapshots.push(Object.freeze([...payload]));
      advance();
    };

    try {
      listener(payload, done);
    } catch (value: unknown) {
      if (!acknowledged) {
        acknowledged = true;
        finish(value instanceof Error ? value : new Error(String(value)));
      }
    }
  };

  advance();
}
