","known_bad_label":"Reuses one mutable payload across listeners, so mutations leak into later listener inputs."},{"id":"cap-v2-callbacks_and_events-typescript-repair-02","problem":"Repair the implementation below and return one complete TypeScript source file.

Export exactly this API:

```ts
export interface Broadcast {
  readonly channel: string;
  readonly labels: readonly string[];
}

export type BroadcastListener = (
  message: Broadcast,
  acknowledge: (error?: Error) => void,
) => void;

export class AcknowledgedBroadcaster {
  subscribe(listener: BroadcastListener): () => void;
  publish(
    message: Broadcast,
    complete: (error: Error | null) => void,
  ): void;
}
```

Each `subscribe` call creates an independent registration and returns an idempotent unsubscribe callback. `publish` must capture the registrations present when publication starts and invoke those listeners once, in registration order. Later subscription changes must not affect that publication.

Every invoked listener must receive its own object containing its own copy of `labels`. Consequently, listener mutations performed through a cast must not change the caller's message or any other listener's message.

A publication completes only after every captured listener has acknowledged or thrown. Repeated acknowledgements from one listener count once. A thrown value is that listener's failure; convert non-`Error` values with `new Error(String(value))`. Call `complete` exactly once, using the failure belonging to the earliest registered failing listener, or `null` if none failed. With no listeners, complete immediately.

The implementation must be self-contained and deterministic. Do not use filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. It must compile under strict TypeScript as CommonJS targeting ES2022.

The current source shares a message object among listeners:

```ts
export interface Broadcast {
  readonly channel: string;
  readonly labels: readonly string[];
}

export type BroadcastListener = (
  message: Broadcast,
  acknowledge: (error?: Error) => void,
) => void;

export class AcknowledgedBroadcaster {
  private readonly listeners: BroadcastListener[] = [];

  subscribe(listener: BroadcastListener): () => void {
    this.listeners.push(listener);
    let active = true;
    return (): void => {
      if (!active) return;
      active = false;
      const index = this.listeners.indexOf(listener);
      if (index >= 0) this.listeners.splice(index, 1);
    };
  }

  publish(
    message: Broadcast,
    complete: (error: Error | null) => void,
  ): void {
    const current = [...this.listeners];
    if (current.length === 0) {
      complete(null);
      return;
    }

    const delivered: Broadcast = {
      channel: message.channel,
      labels: [...message.labels],
    };
    const errors: Array<Error | undefined> = new Array(current.length);
    let remaining = current.length;
    let completed = false;

    const finishOne = (index: number, error?: Error): void => {
      if (error !== undefined) errors[index] = error;
      remaining--;
      if (remaining === 0 && !completed) {
        completed = true;
        complete(errors.find((value): value is Error => value !== undefined) ?? null);
      }
    };

    current.forEach((listener, index) => {
      let acknowledged = false;
      const acknowledge = (error?: Error): void => {
        if (acknowledged) return;
        acknowledged = true;
        finishOne(index, error);
      };

      try {
        listener(delivered, acknowledge);
      } catch (value: unknown) {
        if (!acknowledged) {
          acknowledged = true;
          finishOne(
            index,
            value instanceof Error ? value : new Error(String(value)),
          );
        }
      }
    });
  }
}
