","known_bad_label":"Silently drops links whose parent is absent instead of rejecting the malformed parent reference."},{"id":"cap-v2-graph_and_tree-typescript-generation-02","problem":"Write one complete TypeScript source file implementing the following exact API:

```ts
export interface OutlineRow {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly label: string;
  readonly depth: number;
}

export interface OutlineNode {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly label: string;
  readonly path: readonly string[];
  subtreeSize: number;
  readonly children: OutlineNode[];
}

export function buildOutline(
  rows: readonly OutlineRow[],
): OutlineNode[];
```

Rows encode a forest in preorder. A row at depth `0` starts a root. A row at depth `d > 0` is a child of the most recent row at depth `d - 1`. Siblings retain their input order. Each output node's `path` contains the labels from its root through that node, and `subtreeSize` counts that node and all its descendants.

Depth syntax is strict. Every depth must be a non-negative integer; otherwise throw `new RangeError("Invalid depth at: " + id)`. A nonempty input must begin at depth `0`. A row may stay at the same depth, decrease by any amount, or increase by exactly one, but it must never jump upward by more than one. A bad first depth or upward jump must throw `new RangeError("Invalid depth jump at: " + id)`. Empty input returns an empty array.

The implementation must be self-contained and deterministic. Do not use filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. It must compile under strict TypeScript as CommonJS targeting ES2022.","reference_code":"export interface OutlineRow {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly label: string;
  readonly depth: number;
}

export interface OutlineNode {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly label: string;
  readonly path: readonly string[];
  subtreeSize: number;
  readonly children: OutlineNode[];
}

export function buildOutline(
  rows: readonly OutlineRow[],
): OutlineNode[] {
  const roots: OutlineNode[] = [];
  const stack: OutlineNode[] = [];
  let previousDepth = -1;

  for (const row of rows) {
    if (!Number.isInteger(row.depth) || row.depth < 0) {
      throw new RangeError("Invalid depth at: " + row.id);
    }
    if (row.depth > previousDepth + 1) {
      throw new RangeError("Invalid depth jump at: " + row.id);
    }

    while (stack.length > row.depth) stack.pop();
    const parent = row.depth === 0 ? undefined : stack[row.depth - 1];
    const path = parent === undefined
      ? [row.label]
      : [...parent.path, row.label];
    const node: OutlineNode = {
      id: row.id,
      label: row.label,
      path,
      subtreeSize: 1,
      children: [],
    };

    if (parent === undefined) roots.push(node);
    else parent.children.push(node);

    stack[row.depth] = node;
    stack.length = row.depth + 1;
    previousDepth = row.depth;
  }

  const measure = (node: OutlineNode): number => {
    let size = 1;
    for (const child of node.children) size += measure(child);
    node.subtreeSize = size;
    return size;
  };

  for (const root of roots) measure(root);
  return roots;
}
